        move('Bava Batra 14a:12-14b:1 (read whole at the docket)', "WHAT ELSE THE ARK HELD — THE TWO ARMS: R. MEIR (the cubit SIX handbreadths — the ark 15 × 9 × 9, the two tablets 6 × 6 × 3 laid along the length twelve, the three left half a handbreadth for the walls and two handbreadths for THE TORAH SCROLL INSIDE); R. YEHUDA (the cubit FIVE — 12.5 × 7.5 × 7.5, the tablets twelve of the twelve and a half, the silver columns inside; the scroll on the Philistines' chest BESIDE the ark, 1 Samuel 6:8); 'the tablets and the fragments' the arms agree on")
        move('cold_run_sanctuary_build (CALL) — SB.ark(dimensions) = %s; SB.ark(hidden_with) = %s' % (SB_DIM['v'], SB_HIDDEN['v']), "the spec's cubits (2.5 × 1.5 × 1.5 — the two arms' cubit the parameter) and the ark hidden with the manna jar, the oil and the staff (Yoma 52b — Josiah's hiding, Mishnah Shekalim 6:1-2)")
        dat('THE EFFECT\'S VALUE\'S SECOND PARAMETER — the scroll INSIDE (R. Meir) or BESIDE (R. Yehuda): the value carries both arms; the tablets\' size 6 × 6 × 3 the 7b DATA row (Nedarim 38a:8); the exam\'s row a DISPUTE recorded, not resolved')
